# draftwave.part -- Rounds along ellipses, where drafted faces meet a wave
# Copyright (c) 2026 Jakob Kastelic

# A box 60 by 60 across y, its corners round, of 12 at the back, whose
# faces lean in by a draft of 3 degrees toward its front, so that at the
# front the corners keep a radius of 10.4, room for the round below;
# with a wave across the front: an extrusion along x of an outline in y
# and z whose front runs at y = 0,
# and between z = 15 and 45 steps out to y = -12 in an S of two arcs
# each way, of 2 where it turns in and of 8 where it turns out.  The
# box is what both have in common.  The edge where the faces of the
# box meet the wave turns outward all round, and one round of 5.08
# follows it: along the lines of the planes, round the tori of the
# corners, and where the drafted sides meet the cylinders of the arcs
# at a slant, along ellipses, as pipes, of 7.08 and of 2.92 about their
# axes.
profile blk along y 0 0 12 60 0 12 60 60 12 0 60 12
extrude box from 30 to -14 blk draft 3
profile wv along x 40 -1 0 40 61 0 0 61 0 0 45 2 -12 45 8 -12 15 8 \
    0 15 2 0 -1 0
extrude wave from -1 to 61 wv
common part box wave
round 5.08 box.side wave
